      "Saint Maura": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar remembers Saint Maura on November 10. Maura was a young Christian of third-century Egypt who married Timothy, a village lector who kept the holy Scriptures safe during Diocletian's persecution. Only weeks after their wedding, Timothy was arrested and ordered to surrender the sacred books; he refused, and Maura, pressed to change his mind, chose instead to share his confession of faith. Husband and wife were martyred together around the year 286.": 1,
      "Brief story based on Aleteia's account of Saints Timothy and Maura. The date follows the Maronite calendar.": 1,
      "Read about Saint Maura and Saint Timothy": 1,
      "Feast source: Eparchy of St. Maron liturgical calendar": 5,
