      "Saint Mennas and His Companions": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar remembers Saint Mennas and his companions on November 11. Mennas was an Egyptian soldier serving in Phrygia under the emperors Diocletian and Maximian. Admired for his courage, he left the army to seek God in the desert, and when he openly confessed his faith in Christ he was arrested, tortured and beheaded. His witness spread far beyond Egypt, and pilgrims have honored him for centuries.": 1,
      "Brief story based on the Orthodox Church in America. The date follows the Maronite calendar.": 3,
      "Read about Saint Mennas and his companions": 1,
