      "Saint Theodore the Studite": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar remembers Saint Theodore the Studite on November 12. Born in 759 in Constantinople, Theodore became a monk and later abbot of the Stoudios Monastery, leading a renewal of common prayer, work and learning. He defended the veneration of icons when emperors attacked it and endured exile more than once rather than yield; his letters and teachings guided monks, families and leaders across the Byzantine world.": 1,
      "Brief story based on Wikipedia. The date follows the Maronite calendar.": 1,
      "Read about Saint Theodore the Studite": 1,
      "12.11.2026": 1,
